# Party banter around Old Bonegrinder. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible only while its
# condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections; a line plays if a matching member is present.

~ banter_sails
if not flag.morgantha_home_met and not flag.bonegrinder_burned
interject tag:curious: A windmill with the sails tied down, and the chimney going full blast. What's it grinding, if the wind isn't turning it?
interject tag:blunt: Don't answer that.
interject class:wizard: I wasn't going to. I was going to think it very loudly.
endif
-> END

~ banter_keeper
if flag.ilinca_met and not flag.children_rescued
interject class:cleric: Lycanthropes who worship nothing but keeping watch. I was taught they were all cursed. She seems more tired than cursed.
interject tag:loyal: Most soldiers I've known were both.
endif
-> END

~ banter_coven
if flag.coven_explained and not flag.morgantha_slain
interject name:ilse_varga: Three of them, fight them one at a time. That's not cheating. That's just the only tactics anybody ever needed.
interject name:silvain_aster: It's the first chapter of every treatise on hags, actually. The second chapter is a list of the people who skipped the first.
endif
-> END

~ banter_pastry_taste
if flag.dream_pastry_eaten and flag.offalia_met
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: I ate one of those. In the village. It was the best thing I've eaten in my life, and I've eaten in a duke's larder.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: And now you know where the flour comes from.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: And now I'm never eating anything again. For about an hour.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bella_pact
if flag.bella_pact and not flag.morgantha_slain
interject tag:devout: We've promised a mill full of stolen souls to a hag so that she'll sit out a fight. I keep turning it over to find the side that looks better.
interject tag:blunt: There isn't one. There's the side with the children on it. That'll have to do.
endif
-> END

~ banter_children_out
if flag.children_rescued
interject name:ilse_varga: Two of them, alive, walking down a hill on their own feet. I've had worse days in this trade. Most of them, in fact.
interject tag:cheerful: Toma waved. Did you see? He waved at me.
endif
-> END

~ banter_the_truth
if flag.sarnov_truth_told
interject name:hedda_ironvow: We told a ten-year-old her mother sold her. I've been asking myself whether that was right since the stair.
interject name:silvain_aster: She asked. She'd have known if we lied, and then she'd have known we lied, too. That's two things to carry instead of one.
endif
-> END

~ banter_home_again
if flag.bonegrinder_children_fate == "home"
interject tag:curious: Do you think their mother will buy pastries again?
interject tag:blunt: I think she'll look at every child in the village for the rest of her life. That's not a punishment I'd wish on anyone. She earned it anyway.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bargain
if flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "gold" or flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "truce"
interject tag:blunt: We paid a hag to give back children she stole, and walked out past her oven. Somebody tell me that was the clever thing.
interject class:wizard: It was the living thing. Clever comes second, in this valley.
endif
-> END

~ banter_dream_debt
if flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "dream" and not flag.morgantha_slain
interject tag:curious: The one she took a dream from. Do you know what it was?
interject tag:devout: No. That's the part I can't forgive her. Not the taking. That I don't know what's missing.
endif
-> END

~ banter_another_house
if flag.death_house_children_met and flag.sarnov_children_met
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Another house with children shut in upstairs. Is that every house in Barovia, do you think? Is it the architecture?
interject name:hedda_ironvow: It is the landlord.
endif
-> END

~ banter_kesten
if flag.bone_heap_searched
interject class:cleric: Brother Kesten came up this hill alone with a cudgel and a prayer. I'll wear his symbol a while, so that someone finishes the walk.
endif
-> END

~ banter_keepers
if flag.ilinca_vouched
interject tag:curious: Raven-eyed innkeeper in Vallaki. She meant Urwin, didn't she? The whole family's birds, I'd bet.
interject tag:loyal: Then that's a family that owes us. Good to have, in a place like this.
endif
-> END

~ banter_trade_ended
if flag.pastry_trade == "ended"
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: No more dream pastries anywhere in the valley. Somewhere a lot of people are going to wake up and remember they're sad.
interject name:ilse_varga: Good. Sad people bolt their doors. Dreaming ones don't.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ireena_mill
if guest:ireena and flag.morgantha_home_met
interject guest:ireena: My father bought one of her baskets once, the winter he couldn't sleep. He slept all the next day, smiling. I thought she'd done him a kindness.
interject tag:devout: It was a kindness, from him. Not from her.
endif
-> END
